.TH IB-AGENT 1 "2026-08-11" "ib_agent 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ib-agent \- read-only Interactive Brokers portfolio sync and query CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ib-agent
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B ib-agent
.BR status | sync | positions | expiries | underlyings | show | history | watch
.br
.BR watchlist | instruments | resolve | chain | greeks | orders | executions | gateway
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ib-agent
reads an Interactive Brokers account over the TWS API and stores snapshots in
SQLite. It is the single sanctioned entry point for IBKR data on this machine:
other projects call this command instead of talking to IBKR themselves, so that
credentials, the Gateway session and the read-only guarantee live in one place.
.PP
Reads require no login and no manual approval. IBC keeps one IB Gateway logged
in in the background and every read is a local socket connection to it. If the
Gateway is not running, commands that need it fail rather than prompting.
.PP
Every data command accepts
.BR \-\-json ,
which is the stable machine interface. Human table output is for terminals only
and its layout may change; the JSON payloads are the contract.
.SH SAFETY
The API session cannot place, change or cancel orders. Four independent gates
enforce this:
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
.I ReadOnlyApi=yes
in
.IR ~/ibc/config.ini
\(em the Gateway itself rejects order messages on the API socket.
.IP \(bu 2
.I IB_READONLY=true
\(em the client library refuses order calls.
.IP \(bu 2
no order code exists in the package.
.IP \(bu 2
IBKR user rights withhold Funding and Account Settings from the login the
Gateway uses.
.RE
.PP
No IBKR username or password is stored in this project. They are known only to
IBC, in
.IR ~/ibc/config.ini .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Report whether the Gateway process is running and the API port accepts
connections. Accepts
.BR \-\-json .
This is the cheapest health check and needs no IB session.
.TP
.B sync \fR[\fB\-\-quiet\fR]
Fetch a full snapshot (positions, account values, new instrument
classifications) and store it in SQLite plus a JSON copy under
.IR data/snapshots/ .
.B \-\-quiet
suppresses the table. Accepts
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B positions\fR, \fBpos
List positions with filters, grouping and totals. Reads live from the Gateway by
default.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-stored
Use the last stored snapshot; does not contact IBKR. Instant.
.TP
.B \-\-save
Persist the freshly fetched snapshot.
.TP
.BI \-g " KEY" "\fR, \fB\-\-group-by " KEY
Group rows and subtotal each group:
.IR expiry ,
.IR right ,
.IR underlying ,
.IR sec_type ,
.IR asset_class ,
.IR account ,
.IR side ,
.IR none
(default).
.TP
.BI \-s " KEY" "\fR, \fB\-\-sort " KEY
Sort by
.IR symbol " (default), " expiry ", " dte ", " strike ", " quantity ", " value ", " pnl ", " underlying .
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse the sort, e.g. worst P&L first.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Show at most N rows.
.TP
.B \-\-totals-only
Omit rows, keep totals.
.RE
.TP
.B expiries
Option exposure grouped by expiry: contract count and value per expiry. Accepts
all filters and
.BR \-\-stored / \-\-save .
.TP
.B underlyings
Exposure grouped by underlying symbol. Same options as
.BR expiries .
.TP
.B show
Print the most recent stored snapshot. Never contacts IBKR. Exits non-zero if
nothing is stored yet.
.TP
.B history \fR[\fB\-\-limit \fIN\fR]
List stored snapshots with net liquidation, newest first. Default 20.
.TP
.B watch \fR[\fB\-\-interval \fISECONDS\fR] [\fB\-\-quiet\fR]
Unattended sync loop; default interval 900 seconds. Intended to run as the
single background writer so that readers can use
.B \-\-stored
and pay no IB round trip.
.TP
.B watchlist\fR, \fBwl \fIadd\fR|\fIremove\fR|\fIlist\fR|\fIquotes\fR [\fISYMBOL\fR...]
Manage a locally stored watchlist and quote it. This watchlist lives in this
project's database; it is not an IBKR account watchlist and writing to it cannot
affect the account.
.B quotes
with symbols quotes those symbols ad hoc and ignores the stored list.
Options:
.BR \-\-sec-type " (STK, IND, CASH, FUT, CRYPTO), " \-\-exchange ", " \-\-currency ", " \-\-note .
.TP
.B instruments
Print cached underlying reference data (asset class from IB's
.IR stockType :
ETF, COMMON, ADR; long name, industry, category). Populated as a side effect of
.BR sync ,
one lookup per new underlying.
.TP
.B resolve \fR[\fISPEC\fR...] [\fB\-\-from-positions\fR] [\fB\-\-options\fR] [\fB\-\-stored\fR]
Resolve contracts to IB contract ids. A
.I SPEC
is a bare conid
.RI ( 12345 ),
a symbol
.RI ( GDX ),
a symbol with sec type
.RI ( GDX:STK )
or an option
.RI ( \(dqGDX\ 2026-09-18\ P\ 45\(dq ).
With
.BR \-\-from-positions ,
resolve what is held instead, which reports each option's
.B underlying_con_id
directly from IB rather than inferring it from a symbol. Add
.B \-\-options
to skip equity positions and
.B \-\-stored
to take the position list from the last snapshot. One unresolvable spec is
reported in its own row with
.BR error ;
the rest still resolve.
.TP
.B chain \fISYMBOL\fR [\fB\-e \fIPREFIX\fR] [\fB\-\-strike-min \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-strike-max \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-exchange \fIEXCH\fR]
Option expirations and strikes for one underlying, from
.BR reqSecDefOptParams .
IB answers once per exchange and trading class;
.B \-\-exchange
keeps one (usually SMART).
.B \-e
keeps expirations with a prefix
.RI ( 2026-09 ),
and the strike bounds narrow the strike list. Filtering happens after the
fetch, so the table and
.B \-\-json
always agree.
.TP
.B greeks \fR[\fISPEC\fR...] [filters] [\fB\-\-stored\fR]
Model greeks \(em implied volatility, delta, gamma, theta, vega \(em plus the option
and underlying price IB modelled them at. With no arguments, prices every held
option and totals the book; all position filters apply. With specs, prices those
contracts instead. Each row carries
.B position_delta
(delta times size times multiplier) and
.BR source ,
which names the greek set IB actually returned
.RI ( model ", " last ", " bid ", " ask ).
Contracts with no option market data are still listed, with
.B error
set and greeks null, so a gap is visible rather than silently absent. Exits
.B 4
when nothing could be priced.
.TP
.B orders \fR[\fB\-\-all\fR]
Working orders, read-only: this asks IB what exists and can neither place,
modify nor cancel anything. By default only IB's active statuses
.RI ( ApiPending ", " PendingSubmit ", " PreSubmitted ", " Submitted ", " PendingCancel );
.B \-\-all
also lists orders IB still reports as filled or cancelled. Orders placed
elsewhere \(em IBKR Mobile, for instance \(em belong to another client id and are
relayed only when
.B OverrideTwsMasterClientID
is set in
.IR ~/ibc/config.ini ,
so an empty list is not proof that nothing is working. The JSON payload repeats
that caveat in
.BR master_client_id_hint .
.TP
.B executions\fR, \fBfills \fR[\fB\-\-symbol \fISYM\fR] [\fB\-\-sec-type \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-side \fIBOT\fR|\fISLD\fR]
Today's fills with commission and realized P&L, plus a signed
.B proceeds
per fill (negative when buying). IB's
.B reqExecutions
covers the current trading day only, whatever filter is passed, which the
payload states as
.BR "window: today" .
Older history needs the Flex Web Service
.RB ( IB_FLEX_QUERY_ID ).
.TP
.B gateway \fIup\fR|\fIcode\fR|\fIstatus\fR|\fIdown\fR
Start or stop the headless Gateway via IBC, and complete its two-factor login.
.B up
starts Xvfb and the Gateway, waits for IBKR's
.I Second Factor Authentication
dialog, asks for a 6-digit Mobile Authenticator code at the moment it is needed,
types it on the headless display and waits for the API port. The code is
requested late on purpose: it expires in about 30 seconds, so it cannot be
collected before the dialog exists.
.B code
.I NNNNNN
submits a code to a login that is already waiting and never starts a second
Gateway \(em this is how a session dropped by IBKR's weekly server reset is
refreshed.
.B status
is a synonym for
.BR status .
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-code " NNNNNN"
Submit this code instead of prompting. Only sound when a dialog is already up.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-prompt
Never read stdin; exit
.B 5
if a code is required. For cron and for agents that must ask a human out of band.
.TP
.BI \-\-attempts " N"
How many codes to try before giving up (default 3). A code refused by IBKR is
retried with a fresh one.
.TP
.BI \-\-wait " SECONDS"
How long to wait for the dialog or the port (default 120).
.RE
.PP
One code per session, not per read: once the port is open, every later query is a
local socket connect needing no human. See
.B docs/GATEWAY-LOGIN.md
for failure modes and debugging.
.SH FILTERS
Accepted by
.BR positions ,
.B expiries
and
.BR underlyings .
All filters are AND-ed; all list-valued filters take comma-separated values.
.TP
.BI \-t " LIST" "\fR, \fB\-\-type " LIST
Security types:
.IR stock ", " option ", " fut ", " cash ...
.TP
.BI \-r " LIST" "\fR, \fB\-\-right " LIST
Option right:
.IR put ", " call .
.TP
.BI \-u " LIST" "\fR, \fB\-\-underlying " LIST
Underlying symbols.
.TP
.BI \-a " LIST" "\fR, \fB\-\-asset " LIST
Asset class of the underlying:
.IR etf ", " common ", " adr .
.TP
.BI \-e " LIST" "\fR, \fB\-\-expiry " LIST
Expiry prefix:
.IR 2026-09 ", " 202609 ", " 20260904 .
.TP
.BI \-\-expiry-from " DATE" "\fR, \fB\-\-expiry-to " DATE
ISO date range on expiry.
.TP
.BI \-\-dte-min " N" "\fR, \fB\-\-dte-max " N
Days to expiry bounds.
.TP
.BI \-\-side " long" |
.I short
Long or short positions.
.TP
.B \-\-options\fR, \fB\-\-equities
Shorthand type filters.
.TP
.BI \-\-contains " TEXT"
Substring match on the IB local symbol.
.TP
.BI \-\-account " LIST"
Restrict to account ids.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
With
.BR \-\-json ,
data commands print a single JSON
.I object
on standard output and nothing else; diagnostics go to standard error. Never a
bare array: an array has nowhere to carry the schema version, so a consumer
could not tell which shape it is parsing. Common keys:
.TP
.B schema
Integer contract version, currently 1. Fields are added without a bump;
renaming or removing one bumps it. Refuse a version you do not know.
.TP
.B source
.I live
when fetched from the Gateway,
.I snapshot
when read from storage.
.TP
.B as_of
ISO 8601 timestamp of the data, not of the invocation. Consumers must treat this
as the freshness signal and refuse stale data themselves.
.TP
.B accounts\fR, \fBfilters\fR, \fBtotals
Accounts covered, the filters that were applied, and aggregate figures.
.TP
.B positions
Flat list of position objects, when not grouping.
.TP
.B groups
When grouping:
.BR groups[].key ,
.BR groups[].totals ,
and
.B groups[].positions
unless
.B \-\-totals-only
was given.
.PP
List-shaped commands wrap their rows and add a count:
.B history
returns
.BR snapshots ,
.B instruments
returns
.BR instruments ,
.B watchlist list
returns
.BR watchlist ,
.B resolve
returns
.B contracts
(plus
.B resolved
and
.B failed
counts),
.B chain
returns
.B chains
with
.B expirations
and
.B strikes
per exchange,
.B greeks
returns
.B greeks
with a
.B totals
object holding the book's delta, gamma, theta and vega,
.B orders
returns
.BR orders ,
and
.B executions
returns
.B executions
with
.BR "window: today" .
.PP
Quantities are negative for short positions. A short option position therefore
has negative
.BR market_value ,
and positive
.B unrealized_pnl
means the short option has lost value, which is a gain for the seller.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Read from the process environment and from
.I .env
in the project root.
.TP
.B IB_HOST
Gateway host. Default
.IR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.B IB_PORT
API port. Default
.IR 4001 .
4002 and 7497 are paper ports and select paper mode.
.TP
.B IB_CLIENT_ID
TWS API client id. Default
.IR 17 .
Concurrent invocations sharing one client id collide on the Gateway; give
long-running processes a distinct id.
.TP
.B IB_ACCOUNT
Restrict every read to one account id. Empty means all managed accounts.
.TP
.B IB_READONLY
Default
.IR true .
Keep it true.
.TP
.B IB_CONNECT_TIMEOUT
Seconds to wait for the Gateway. Default
.IR 20 .
.TP
.B IB_AUTO_START_GATEWAY
Whether commands may start the Gateway themselves. Default
.IR true .
.TP
.B IB_MARKET_DATA_TYPE
1 live, 2 frozen, 3 delayed, 4 delayed-frozen. Default
.IR 3 ,
which returns real-time data for subscribed products and free delayed data
otherwise, so a quote never fails for lack of a subscription.
.TP
.B IB_DATA_DIR\fR, \fBIB_DB_PATH
Snapshot and database locations. Default
.I data/
and
.I data/portfolio.sqlite3
under the project root.
.TP
.B IB_FLEX_TOKEN\fR, \fBIB_FLEX_QUERY_ID
Flex Web Service credentials, for statement history the TWS API does not expose.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The code says why a command failed, so a caller can decide whether retrying
could possibly help.
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Unexpected runtime failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error from argument parsing.
.TP
.B 3
Gateway unreachable or not logged in. Retrying later may succeed; retrying
immediately will not.
.TP
.B 4
No data: nothing stored yet, or an empty watchlist. Retrying changes nothing
until something syncs. Commands that can still emit a well-formed but empty
payload do so before exiting 4.
.TP
.B 5
A login is waiting for a two-factor code that only the human can supply. Distinct
from 3 on purpose: the Gateway is starting correctly, so a scheduler should ask a
person rather than back off and retry. Answer with
.B gateway code
.IR NNNNNN .
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I data/portfolio.sqlite3
Snapshots, positions, account values, instruments, watchlist.
.TP
.I data/snapshots/portfolio-*.json
Human-readable copy of each snapshot.
.TP
.I .env
Local settings; see ENVIRONMENT.
.TP
.I ~/ibc/config.ini
IBC configuration, including the IBKR credentials and
.IR ReadOnlyApi .
Not read by this program.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Check the Gateway before doing anything else:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ib-agent status --json
.EE
.RE
.PP
The option book by expiry, with a subtotal per expiry:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ib-agent positions --options --group-by expiry
.EE
.RE
.PP
Short puts on ETF underlyings expiring within a month, nearest first:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ib-agent positions --right put --asset etf --dte-max 30 --sort dte
.EE
.RE
.PP
Assignment risk review \(em everything expiring within two weeks:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ib-agent positions --dte-max 14 --sort dte --json
.EE
.RE
.PP
Worst unrealized P&L first:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ib-agent positions --sort pnl --reverse --limit 10
.EE
.RE
.PP
Book-level greek exposure, and the delta of every short put:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ib-agent greeks --json | jq .totals
ib-agent greeks --right put --side short
.EE
.RE
.PP
Underlying conid for every held option, which is what a consumer keys on:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ib-agent resolve --from-positions --options --json \e
  | jq '.contracts[] | {symbol, con_id, underlying_con_id}'
.EE
.RE
.PP
September strikes near the money on one underlying:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ib-agent chain GDX -e 2026-09 --strike-min 40 --strike-max 55 --exchange SMART
.EE
.RE
.PP
What is working right now, and what filled today:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ib-agent orders --json
ib-agent executions --json | jq .totals
.EE
.RE
.PP
Read the stored snapshot without touching IBKR, for a UI request path:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ib-agent positions --stored --json
.EE
.RE
.PP
Quote symbols that are not on the stored watchlist:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ib-agent watchlist quotes TSM ASML --json
.EE
.RE
.PP
Filter grouped JSON with jq:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ib-agent expiries --json | jq '.groups[] | select(.count > 10)'
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES FOR OTHER PROGRAMS
.IP \(bu 2
Prefer
.B \-\-stored
in a request path. A live fetch costs roughly three seconds because it opens a
fresh Gateway connection; the stored read costs nothing and is refreshed by
.B watch
in the background.
.IP \(bu 2
Always pass
.BR \-\-json ,
parse standard output only, and branch on the exit status rather than on text.
.IP \(bu 2
Check
.B as_of
and reject data older than your tolerance instead of assuming freshness.
.IP \(bu 2
Do not read
.I data/portfolio.sqlite3
directly. The schema migrates; the JSON payloads are the supported interface.
.IP \(bu 2
Do not call the Gateway or the IBKR Client Portal directly from another project.
Route it through this command so the read-only guarantee and the audit trail
hold.
